# Testing

The X9C104P library has been tested with an Arduino Uno and an X9C104P digital potentiometer.

## Manual Position-Control Test

The test sequence is:

1. Initialize the library.
2. Home the wiper to position 0.
3. Set the position to 25.
4. Set the position to 50.
5. Return the position to 0.

## Observed Results

In the reported voltage-sweep configuration, the approximate wiper voltages were:

| Position | Observed Voltage |
|---:|---:|
| 25 | 1.3 V |
| 50 | 2.6 V |
| 0 | Approximately 0 V |

These measurements describe the tested circuit and are not guaranteed values for other configurations.

## Notes

- Resistance is estimated from the requested position.
- The software tracker does not measure the physical resistance.
- Hardware supply and terminal voltages must remain within the device specifications.